2026-06-01 11:09:26,011 - INFO - Rep 1: Generated argument: Protecting Internet access is essential because it now functions like a basic public utility. Americans rely on it to apply for jobs, attend school, access telehealth, receive government services, and participate in civic debate. Without reliable access, low-income and rural communities are shut out of opportunities and democratic participation. Safeguarding this right does not mean unlimited free service in every circumstance, but it does mean ensuring people cannot be arbitrarily denied meaningful access to the digital world. In modern society, excluding someone from the Internet can be nearly as harmful as excluding them from electricity or transportation.
